# Factory activation checklist

The factory remains unsealed and under qualification. Complete this checklist before authorizing unattended operation through product Phases 1–5. Detailed evidence and the invariant audit live in `factory/qualification.md`; controlled tests do not replace live lifecycle proof.

## 1. Install and test scheduled automation

- [x] Enable GitHub Issues so the factory can persist control and worker state.
- [x] Start or recover the persistent chief-of-staff thread with an explicit maximum implementation concurrency.
- [x] Confirm fresh startup and recovery report readiness and wait for an explicit assignment without launching work.
- [ ] Authorize a bounded automation qualification run before installing or dispatching automations.
- [ ] From that active thread, run `factory.prepare-automations` and copy the private webhook URL from its dialog.
- [ ] Run `bin/install-factory-automations` locally with owner authority to store the webhook secret and enable the repository automation variable.
- [ ] Manually dispatch `.github/workflows/automations.yml` and confirm the webhook wakes the correct chief thread.
- [x] Confirm an hourly run delayed past minute zero still selects the intended hourly slot.
- [ ] Deliver the same webhook event more than once and confirm each event/automation pair launches at most one paid run.
- [ ] Fill each suggestion queue and the implementation queue, then confirm finding-producing automation records `SKIPPED` without launching an orb.
- [ ] Force an automation failure and confirm it records `FAILED`, Amp usage or explicit unavailability, and retries only within the agent's attempt limit.
- [ ] Force completion-record persistence to fail, retry delivery, and confirm the factory recovers the completed thread rather than launching another paid run.
- [ ] Confirm the control issue durably records automation attempt, status, thread ID, elapsed time, and Amp usage.
- [ ] Confirm loop health can consume those durable records.

Completion criterion: manual and scheduled delivery, delayed starts, duplicate delivery, backpressure, bounded retry, recovery, and durable accounting all pass without duplicate paid work.

Startup evidence (2026-09-05): control issue #4 records chief thread `T-01a06e11-ff37-7193-bd63-40f47e1e8dee` and concurrency 1. The chief reported prepared and waiting at `e585236`, with no workers or automations launched. CI passed at that head. Startup recovered the reservation left by a failed orb launch; existing-chief recovery returned the same thread and capacity without appending another startup message after switching the local recovery path to CLI transcript export. The direct plugin transcript API rejects unconnected remote threads. GitHub variable installation and branch-protection checks use owner-side credentials because the orb integration returned 403 for those reads.

## 2. Qualify the complete implementation-issue lifecycle

Use real GitHub state and an independently mergeable qualification issue. Keep one implementation issue mapped to one persistent worker.

- [ ] Confirm the chief creates an implementation issue only while configured worker capacity is available.
- [x] Confirm activation applies both `factory:implementation` and `factory:active` labels.
- [ ] Confirm the worker runs in a fresh mise-backed Amp orb and installs pinned tooling and plugin dependencies.
- [ ] Confirm later attempts resume the same worker thread rather than creating another worker.
- [ ] Cause a deterministic check to fail and confirm the worker receives a bounded retry.
- [ ] Reach attempt three and confirm the worker is directed to read `docs/MISTAKES.md` before continuing.
- [ ] Produce reviewer feedback and confirm it returns to the persistent worker for revision.
- [ ] Change the pull-request head during or after review and confirm the stale review cannot authorize merge.
- [ ] Confirm the changed head reruns CI and receives a fresh independent review.
- [ ] Create a real merge conflict and confirm a fresh conflict-resolver orb handles it.
- [ ] Confirm conflict resolution changes require another current-head CI and review cycle.
- [ ] Confirm failed or incomplete checks block merge regardless of model judgment.
- [ ] Confirm an accepting review is bound to the exact current head, issue, reviewer thread, prompt, generation, and response provenance.
- [ ] Confirm merge succeeds only through `factory_merge_pull_request` after every deterministic gate passes.
- [ ] Confirm merge removes `factory:active` and records total worker usage.
- [ ] Restart or interrupt the controller and confirm GitHub state recovers the worker, attempt, PR, and control reservations.
- [x] Exercise startup reservation recovery and confirm it neither duplicates the chief nor loses the durable control issue.
- [ ] Exercise the full attempt budget in a disposable qualification case and confirm exhaustion records `FACTORY_BLOCKED`, reports an interminable blocker, records worker usage, and halts further attempts.

Completion criterion: the evidence covers retries, feedback, stale heads, conflicts, CI, merge, restart recovery, reservation recovery, and exhaustion. No path creates a second worker for one issue or merges from stale evidence.

## 3. Validate fresh and resumed orb environments

- [ ] Run implementation, review, conflict-resolution, QA, bug-finding, factory-improvement, and maintenance roles through their repository-owned agent definitions.
- [x] Confirm every non-chief role uses `executor: "orb"`.
- [ ] Confirm fresh orbs run `factory/orb/setup`, use pinned mise tools, and run `npm ci` for the factory plugin.
- [ ] Confirm resumed orbs run `factory/orb/resume` and verify the prepared environment within Amp's ten-second wait, without reinstalling dependencies.
- [ ] Run `bin/check-dev-env` from a clean orb.
- [ ] Run `mise run linecount:factory` and `mise run linecount:projects` from a clean orb.
- [ ] Import and typecheck the plugin from a clean orb.
- [x] Confirm the main project receives no DMS credentials.
- [ ] Confirm twin-validation receives only `DEADMANSNITCH_API_KEY`.
- [ ] Confirm holdout-validation receives only `MCP_DEADMANSNITCH_HOLDOUT_TOKEN`.
- [ ] Confirm logs, errors, reports, transcripts, and durable status records reveal no credential values.

Completion criterion: fresh and resumed execution produce the same passing checks while maintaining the three-project credential boundary.

Existing-chief evidence (2026-09-05, `e4e5bf2`): setup passed in 24.773 s; two explicit resume runs passed in 1.027 s and 1.045 s; direct `bin/check-dev-env` passed in 6.146 s. Both line-count tasks passed, and the working tree remained clean. Explicit environment-membership checks showed both credential variables absent in the normal shell and under mise; an earlier model report misinterpreted redacted output and was corrected. CI passed. A fresh orb and automatic wake still need verification. Direct CLI and built-in mode-discovery attempts could not launch the runtime-registered reviewer mode; no review orb was created and independent review remains outstanding.

## 4. Add later dispatcher coverage only when executable

The checked automation configuration currently accepts only cron-driven work executable in the main Amp project. Unsupported project or event routes are rejected instead of silently delegated.

- [ ] During the twin/conformance phase, add an executable twin-validation dispatcher for bounded live differential work.
- [ ] Confirm only that dispatcher receives the factory-owned DMS key.
- [ ] Confirm live runs create bounded owned records, clean them in the same run, halt on leftovers, and never mutate records they did not create.
- [ ] During holdout qualification, add the required holdout-validation dispatch path without exposing the DMS key.
- [ ] During the release phase, add release-pull-request event dispatch only after the release workflow is no longer a placeholder.
- [ ] Extend `factory/check.mjs` whenever a new project or trigger becomes executable so unsupported routes continue to fail closed.

Completion criterion: every configured route has a real dispatcher, correct project isolation, bounded runtime, durable status, and an explicit output destination. No configuration entry returns a delegated placeholder.

